-- title:
--   Monic Casimir relations on the GL₃ smoothing module
-- statement:
--   Fix a character $\omega$ of the idèle units of $\mathbb{Q}$ with all values of absolute value $1$, and a continuous $f : GL_3(\mathbb{A}_\mathbb{Q}) \to \mathbb{C}$ that is left invariant under the image of $GL_3(\mathbb{Q})$, transforms by $\omega$ under central adelic scalars, is of moderate growth in the sense that $\|f\| \le C\,\mathrm{gauge3}^N$ on the whole group, has vanishing integrals over the two two-dimensional unipotent radicals `radicalP21`, `radicalP12` against the conditional adelic Haar measure attached to the pins `productionPinsOf ℚ ∅ (fun _ => ⊥) (fun _ => 1) (AdelicBox.adelicBox ℚ)`, is smooth in the archimedean matrix entries off the vanishing locus of the determinant, and has the property that the right translates $g \mapsto f(gk)$, for $k$ trivial at every finite place and orthogonal at infinity, all lie in the span of one fixed finite set. Let $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,n \to \mathbb{C}$ and $t : \mathrm{Fin}\,n \to GL_3(\mathbb{A}_\mathbb{Q})$ with each $t_i$ trivial at infinity be such that $v(x) = \sum_i c_i f(x t_i)$ is centre-finite, i.e. annihilated by a monic polynomial in each of the three archimedean operators `casimir1`, `casimir2`, `casimir3` (the traces of one, two and three right derivatives `archDeriv`). Let $u$ lie in the span of the functions obtained by applying a word of operators `archDeriv` to $g \mapsto \sum_i c_i f(g h t_i)$ for some $h$. Further data are given: an injective family of exponents $e : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \mathbb{C}$, coefficient functions $a_{ij}$ continuous on $\{y>0\}\times GL_3(\mathbb{A}_\mathbb{Q})$, an exponent $\tau > 1/2$, and the hypothesis that the Whittaker coefficient `whittaker3` of $u$ with respect to the standard additive character $\psi_\mathbb{Q}$, evaluated at $\mathrm{diag}(y_1y_2,y_2,1)k$, is approximated by $\sum_{i,j} a_{ij}(y_2,k)\,y_1^{e_i}(\log y_1)^j$ with error $O(y_1^{\tau})$ uniformly for $k$ in a compact set and $y_2$ in a compact subinterval of $(0,\infty)$, together with an index $i_0$ with $\mathrm{Re}\,e_{i_0} = 1/2$. The conclusion asserts, for the module $M$ spanned by the smoothings $\mathrm{smoothingOperator}\,\varphi\,u = \int \varphi(g)u(\cdot\,g)\,dg$ over those $\varphi$ that are smoothing kernels (a smooth compactly supported archimedean factor supported where the determinant is nonzero, times the indicator of a compact open level subgroup, almost all of whose local factors are the standard maximal compact) whose left translates $g \mapsto \varphi(k^{-1}g)$ for $k$ finite-trivial and orthogonal at infinity lie in the span of one fixed finite set: there exist degrees $N_1,N_2,N_3$ and monic coefficient families $a_1,a_2,a_3$ (top coefficient $1$) such that $\sum_l a_{c,l}\,\mathrm{casimir}_c^{\,l}$ kills the Whittaker coefficient of every $w \in M$ for $c = 1,2,3$; and, separately, such a monic triple killing every $w \in M$ itself.
--
--   This is the centre-finiteness (annihilation by monic polynomials in the three archimedean Casimir-type operators) of the smoothing module generated by $u$, and of its Whittaker coefficients, in the $GL_3$ stage of the cubic induction. It feeds the assembly statement `exists_smoothingSubmodule_leadingCoeff_form_of_expCoeff_re_eq_one_half_centreFinite_mg`, where this module together with the leading-coefficient map of the $y_1$-expansion provides the required witnesses.
